@startuml backend-use-cases
!pragma layout smetana
title Backend UML — implemented use cases
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #526580
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #EEF4FF
skinparam usecaseBorderColor #365880
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 65

actor Visitor
actor "Authenticated user" as User
actor "Organization owner" as Owner
actor "Local model service\n(Ollama)" as Ollama
actor "Isolated sandbox\nrunner" as Runner
Owner --|> User

rectangle "SovereignForge backend · /api/v1" {
  usecase "Sign up / sign in" as Login
  usecase "Manage own profile\nand sessions / sign out" as Account
  usecase "Create / list workspaces\nand upload / list / remove files" as Files
  usecase "Create / list knowledge bases\nand ingest documents" as Ingest
  usecase "Search knowledge" as Search
  usecase "Chat with a local model" as Chat
  usecase "Submit an AI task" as Submit
  usecase "Analyze documents /\nanswer grounded questions" as Analyze
  usecase "Repair and verify code" as Code
  usecase "Compare procurement quotations\nand generate recommendations" as Procurement
  usecase "Run code verification" as Verify
  usecase "Inspect task status / steps;\ncancel or retry a task" as Track
  usecase "Preview / download artifacts\nand inspect audit events" as Results
  usecase "List models / check health" as Models
  usecase "Register / enable /\ndisable models" as ManageModels
  usecase "Inspect sovereignty status\nand run egress test" as Security
}

Visitor -- Login
User -- Account
User -- Files
User -- Ingest
User -- Search
User -- Chat
User -- Submit
User -- Track
User -- Results
User -- Models
User -- Security
Owner -- ManageModels

Analyze -|> Submit
Code -|> Submit
Procurement -|> Submit
Code ..> Verify : <<include>>
Chat -- Ollama
Ingest -- Ollama
Search -- Ollama
Analyze -- Ollama
Code -- Ollama
Procurement -- Ollama
Verify -- Runner

note bottom of Submit
  Specialized workflows use the same POST /tasks endpoint.
  Dispatch depends on task mode, goal and supplied inputs.
  Authenticated use cases require a valid session.
end note
note bottom of ManageModels
  Owner role is checked for model registration
  and enable/disable operations.
end note
legend bottom
  Solid line = actor participation. Hollow triangle = specialization.
  <<include>> = required behavior for a successful coding workflow.
  No human-review/resume use case is claimed: it is not an exposed route.
  Infrastructure storage and public health probes are omitted for readability.
endlegend
@enduml
